Subject: Lower guzzlehttp/guzzle and pear/crypt_gpg floors to match trixie

Upstream's composer.json requires guzzlehttp/guzzle ^7.10.0 and
pear/crypt_gpg ~1.7.0. Debian trixie ships php-guzzlehttp-guzzle 7.9.2-0.1
and php-crypt-gpg 1.6.11-1, both below those floors, so pkg-php-tools
would otherwise generate an unsatisfiable Depends.

This is judged safe as of the pinned upstream commit: guzzle 7.10.0's
only changelog entry is "Support for PHP 8.5" (irrelevant on trixie's
PHP 8.4), and crypt_gpg 1.7.0 only replaces an internal PEAR dependency
(console_commandline) that Roundcube's enigma plugin never references
directly (verified by grepping for PinCliParameters/SimpleCliWrapper/
Console_CommandLine - no hits in plugins/ or program/).

CAUTION for whoever next bumps the pinned Roundcube version: this
assumption is about the *currently pinned* upstream commit only. If a
future Roundcube release starts actually calling guzzle or crypt_gpg
APIs that only exist in the newer floors upstream declares, this patch
would silently make the package build against a too-old library instead
of failing loudly. Re-check both projects' changelogs between the old
and new pinned commit before assuming this patch still applies as-is.

Forwarded: not-needed
---
Index: rc-build/composer.json
===================================================================
--- rc-build.orig/composer.json
+++ rc-build/composer.json
@@ -5,12 +5,12 @@
     "require": {
         "php": ">=8.1 <8.6",
         "bacon/bacon-qr-code": "^3.0.0",
-        "guzzlehttp/guzzle": "^7.10.0",
+        "guzzlehttp/guzzle": "^7.9.2",
         "guzzlehttp/promises": "^2.0",
         "league/commonmark": "^2.7",
         "masterminds/html5": "~2.9.0",
         "pear/auth_sasl": "~1.2.0",
-        "pear/crypt_gpg": "~1.7.0",
+        "pear/crypt_gpg": "~1.6.3",
         "pear/mail_mime": "~1.10.11",
         "pear/net_sieve": "~1.4.7",
         "pear/net_smtp": "~1.12.0",
